# Laptop Exec — hybrid routing

`~/mounts/` is optional SSHFS (may be STALE for **git** truth). Mount Cursor tools
are ALLOWED. Prefer the table (measured 2026-07-26 load + multi-round).

## Priority by action (source of truth — measured 2026-07-26)

| Action | 1st | 2nd | 3rd | Parallel (same turn) |
|--------|-----|-----|-----|----------------------|
| **Read** | Cursor Read on `/mounts/` | windows-mcp `FileSystem` (abs) | `laptop-exec read` | mount **~16–32**; MCP **~8–12**; LE **≤4** |
| **Grep (content)** | Cursor Grep on `/mounts/` | MCP PowerShell `Select-String` | `laptop-exec rg` | mount **~16–32**; Select-String **~4–8**; LE **≤4** |
| **Glob / filename** | windows-mcp `FileSystem` search/list | Cursor Glob / mount `ls` | `laptop-exec run` | MCP **~8–12**; mount **~16** |
| **Write / Edit / StrReplace / Delete** | windows-mcp `FileSystem` write | Cursor on `/mounts/` | `laptop-exec write` | MCP **~8–10**; mount **~10**; LE **≤4** |
| **git** | `laptop-exec git` **only** | — | — | ≤4 LE |
| **Shell build/test** | windows-mcp `PowerShell` | `laptop-exec run` | mount Shell OK | MCP free / LE ≤4 |
| **UI / Screenshot** | windows-mcp only | — | — | MCP free |

**Notes:** FileSystem search ≠ content Grep (use Select-String). MCP relative → Desktop (use absolute under project root). MCP Read throughput plateaus ~28 rps — prefer ≤~12 parallel MCP reads. Mount Read scales under ×64 in benches.

Evidence (approx): cold Read mount≪MCP≪LE; Write MCP≪mount≪LE; paired load Read mount first 20/20.

## Parallel (maximize)

Fan out independent ops in one turn to the caps above. Never serial-drip. LE hard cap 8 slots (prefer ≤4). Mount/MCP have no mux cap.

## Hooks allow / deny

| Tool on `/mounts/` | Hook |
|---|---|
| Read / Write / Edit / StrReplace / Delete / EditNotebook / Shell / **Grep** / **Glob** | **ALLOW** |
| Task | **ALLOW** (child must paste priority block) |

Project `hooks.json` must stay `{"version":1,"hooks":{}}`.

## FAIL-FAST (windows-mcp)

- **Ready** = tools listed (`windows-mcp` / `user-windows-mcp` with `FileSystem`/`PowerShell`).
- One MCP failure (`ECONNREFUSED`, fetch failed, not connected) → MCP **down for this session** → use mount + `laptop-exec`. Never retry the same MCP call.
- `user-filesystem` ≠ windows-mcp. FileSystem uses `mode=` (not `action=`).

## Paths

- Mount / Cursor tools: `/home/$USER/mounts/PROJECT/REL`
- windows-mcp: absolute Windows under project root (`LAPTOP_REMOTE_PATH` / `rpath|REMOTE_PATH` + REL)
- `laptop-exec`: repo-relative + `-p PROJECT` (never `/home/.../mounts/...`)
- `laptop-exec rg`: **no** `-i`/`-l`/`-n`/`--glob` (rejected)

## Mux / sudo

`laptop-exec` shares 8 SSH slots — prefer ≤4 parallel. Mount/MCP have no that cap.
Sudo: `sudo-from-laptop --smart|--sepidz -- …` — never ask for a password.
